{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1275411-beasts-innate-power","id":1275411,"title":"Beasts' Innate Power","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Onyx Path Worlds","Scion"],"posts":[{"date":"2018-12-19T17:41:42-08:00","id":1275411,"title":"Beasts' Innate Power","content":"Does Beasts\u2019 innate power seem rather meh to anyone else? Other purviews get a useful innate, like Death\u2019s ability talk to ghosts and detect portals to the Underworld, but Beasts just gets protection from mundane, non-controlled animals. Since most animals in the wild avoid humans anyway, and scions would hardly have any difficulty dealing with normal animals, it\u2019s seems a rather useless power. Maybe some campaigns have regular occurrences where scions find themselves in jungles where a tiger decides to attack them for some reason, or there\u2019s a rabies outbreak among the dogs in an African village, but it\u2019s not the kind of thing that comes up regularly in my games.<br /> <br /> In my game, I think I\u2019ll take the Leader of the Pack boon and add that to the innate. The scion can then use their socials on the animal as normal, perhaps with a limit based on legend as to when the animal loses interest and wanders off.<br /> <br /> I\u2019d replace the Leader of the Pack with a boon that calls a mundane animal, or animals, depending on their size/power and the scion\u2019s legend. The type of animal would have to be present with the area \u2013 say legend miles (so no calling penguins in the arctic), and shows up because fate organized for them to be there when the legend was imbued, and stays for the Scene or until un-imbued. The scion is then left to convince them to do whatever he has in mind using the (new) innate and whatever social powers he can bring to bear.<br /> <br /> Discussion?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/972-fairlyhyperman","name":"Fairlyhyperman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar972_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"33"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-20T05:33:42-08:00","id":1275476,"title":"","content":"Depends on the campaign, really, but comparisons to real world animal behavior isn't all that useful. Animals are going to be as aggressive or non-aggressive as the GM desires. Bears, sharks, guard dogs, escaped tigers, rabid animals, startled snakes or spiders, and other such things are stuff that a character with Beasts doesn't have to worry about. Seems useful to me.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3961-thrythlind","name":"Thrythlind","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"214"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-20T06:00:02-08:00","id":1275480,"title":"","content":"It also has the added benefit of providing a motif to work Marvels with.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/18560-saedar","name":"saedar","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"35"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-20T06:46:47-08:00","id":1275491,"title":"","content":"The user only gets a Beasts motif if they take a sacred animal to specialize in, and changing the innate doesn't affect that in any way.<br /> <br /> Regarding utility; sure, if your campaign operates under the premise that mundane animals are hyper-aggressive, then I don't see a problem with the innate as written. Even then, I doubt that a legend 1 hero would have so much difficulty coping with a mundane animal that they'd need a special power to do it. I suppose there may be some use to animals not be able to attack a Beasts user (even when he's attacking them?) if the GM put a pack of rabid dogs in the band's path. Since the innate doesn't affect controlled or Legendary animals (and what constitutes &quot;controlled&quot;? If I got a +1 attitude shift on the animal through a power, are they considered controlled?), I still think it's an innate with extremely limited application. Each to his own.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":972,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/972-fairlyhyperman","user":"Fairlyhyperman","date":". 12-20-2018, 10:13 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/972-fairlyhyperman","name":"Fairlyhyperman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar972_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"33"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-20T15:12:29-08:00","id":1275641,"title":"","content":"If you choose to specialize, does that limit the innate?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thoughts ripple out, birthing others","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1624-falleneco","name":"FallenEco","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1624_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1927"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-20T15:17:56-08:00","id":1275643,"title":"","content":"The thought process behind innates is less that they\u2019re cool in their own right and more that it\u2019s supposed to cover the boring stuff you need for the cool effects (so someone buying pyrokinetic boons doesn\u2019t need to waste a boon on not getting burned by their own powers). The Beast Purview Innate covers the general dealing with animals that all the cool effects build off of.<br /> <br /> If it\u2019s comparatively less cool it\u2019s because dealing with animals is probably only something you\u2019re going to bother with if you\u2019re dealing in the Beast Purview, unlike breathing underwater or being fireproof or seeing ghosts which would be more likely to come up anyway. I don\u2019t really see a solution for that though.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":1098,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","user":"glamourweaver","date":". 12-20-2018, 07:06 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-20T17:04:46-08:00","id":1275664,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1275411-beasts-innate-power?p=1275643#post1275643\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The thought process behind innates is less that they\u2019re cool in their own right and more that it\u2019s supposed to cover the boring stuff you need for the cool effects (so someone buying pyrokinetic boons doesn\u2019t need to waste a boon on not getting burned by their own powers). The Beast Purview Innate covers the general dealing with animals that all the cool effects build off of.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd accept that if it weren't for the fact that you need to buy a boon just to talk to animals in the first place. Unless all other boons just involve channeling aspects of animals, or perhaps brute force mind-controlling them, you're going to have to communicate with them at some point; in which case Leader of the Pack is a mandatory boon.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":972,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/972-fairlyhyperman","user":"Fairlyhyperman","date":". 12-20-2018, 08:10 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/972-fairlyhyperman","name":"Fairlyhyperman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar972_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"33"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-20T17:20:14-08:00","id":1275666,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Fairlyhyperman</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1275411-beasts-innate-power?p=1275664#post1275664\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'd accept that if it weren't for the fact that you need to buy a boon just to talk to animals in the first place. Unless all other boons just involve channeling aspects of animals, or perhaps brute force mind-controlling them, you're going to have to communicate with them at some point; in which case Leader of the Pack is a mandatory boon.</div> </div> </div> </div>I could see folding Leader of the Pack into the innate. I\u2019ll consider it for my own table.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-20T17:34:10-08:00","id":1275671,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>FallenEco</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1275411-beasts-innate-power?p=1275641#post1275641\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If you choose to specialize, does that limit the innate?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I'd think that specializations don't limit the innate, otherwise it'd be even less use.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/972-fairlyhyperman","name":"Fairlyhyperman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar972_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"33"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-20T17:55:16-08:00","id":1275673,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Fairlyhyperman</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1275411-beasts-innate-power?p=1275671#post1275671\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> I'd think that specializations don't limit the innate, otherwise it'd be even less use.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't necessarily think that is true. My read is that it IS limiting, but that's ok. If a character at the table has Beasts (Marmot), I would expect part of the fun would be for the players and Storyguide to find out interesting ways for marmots and/or marmot-like characteristics to be useful. Like... Marmot Girl.<br /> <br /> ...Now I want to make that character...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":18560,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/18560-saedar","user":"saedar","date":". 12-20-2018, 09:01 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/18560-saedar","name":"saedar","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"35"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-20T18:00:33-08:00","id":1275683,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Fairlyhyperman</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1275411-beasts-innate-power?p=1275671#post1275671\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> I'd think that specializations don't limit the innate, otherwise it'd be even less use.</div> </div> </div> </div>Specialization limits the usefulness of everything else in a purview (in return for the Motif). Why would the Innate be different from all the Boons or possible Marvels in that regard?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-20T18:19:02-08:00","id":1275692,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1275411-beasts-innate-power?p=1275683#post1275683\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Specialization limits the usefulness of everything else in a purview (in return for the Motif). Why would the Innate be different from all the Boons or possible Marvels in that regard?</div> </div> </div> </div>You're right, and I guess that's fine with Artistry and Passion's innates, and would be fine if Beasts' innate as currently written didn't just limit you to not being attacked by marmots <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/972-fairlyhyperman","name":"Fairlyhyperman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar972_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"33"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-20T18:23:50-08:00","id":1275694,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Fairlyhyperman</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1275411-beasts-innate-power?p=1275692#post1275692\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> You're right, and I guess that's fine with Artistry and Passion's innates, and would be fine if Beasts' innate as currently written didn't just limit you to not being attacked by marmots <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>They're very fierce, I assure you. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/18560-saedar","name":"saedar","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"35"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-20T18:26:57-08:00","id":1275695,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Fairlyhyperman</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1275411-beasts-innate-power?p=1275692#post1275692\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> You're right, and I guess that's fine with Artistry and Passion's innates, and would be fine if Beasts' innate as currently written didn't just limit you to not being attacked by marmots <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>I\u2019m inclined to allow simple concept communication at an animal\u2019s own realistic cognitive level as part of the innate. Leader of the Pack then enhances that to the animals you communicate with or command understanding much more complex ideas and directions than would be realistic.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-21T14:51:02-08:00","id":1275907,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>saedar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1275411-beasts-innate-power?p=1275673#post1275673\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't necessarily think that is true. My read is that it IS limiting, but that's ok. If a character at the table has Beasts (Marmot), I would expect part of the fun would be for the players and Storyguide to find out interesting ways for marmots and/or marmot-like characteristics to be useful. Like... Marmot Girl.<br /> <br /> ...Now I want to make that character...</div> </div> </div> </div>Literally how Squirrel girl worked.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thoughts ripple out, birthing others","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1624-falleneco","name":"FallenEco","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1624_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1927"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-21T22:51:31-08:00","id":1276018,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Fairlyhyperman</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1275411-beasts-innate-power#post1275411\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Does Beasts\u2019 innate power seem rather meh to anyone else? Other purviews get a useful innate, like Death\u2019s ability talk to ghosts and detect portals to the Underworld, but Beasts just gets protection from mundane, non-controlled animals. Since most animals in the wild avoid humans anyway, and scions would hardly have any difficulty dealing with normal animals, it\u2019s seems a rather useless power. Maybe some campaigns have regular occurrences where scions find themselves in jungles where a tiger decides to attack them for some reason, or there\u2019s a rabies outbreak among the dogs in an African village, but it\u2019s not the kind of thing that comes up regularly in my games.<br /> <br /> In my game, I think I\u2019ll take the Leader of the Pack boon and add that to the innate. The scion can then use their socials on the animal as normal, perhaps with a limit based on legend as to when the animal loses interest and wanders off.<br /> <br /> <br /> Discussion?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Remember the fact that your characters are living legends for whom Fate itself conspires against.<br /> <br /> How many stories, legends and myths can you think of that involve the characters engaging with malicious animals in some form or another?<br /> <br /> One of Hercules' very first demonstrations of his divine powers is when Hera tries to kill him as an infant with a pair of snakes.<br /> <br /> Ordinary, every day humans might not have much to worry about in regards to wild animal attacks. But Scions are a different story, since the Powers That Be have taken an active interest in their lives.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","user":"Nyrufa","date":". 12-22-2018, 01:59 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-21T23:02:26-08:00","id":1276020,"title":"","content":"It's also thematically awesome as well. Yes, Epic Strength lets you toss a car at someone and that <i>seems</i> cooler, because it's a combat-useful power, but the innate power of Beasts will make you look like what you are; someone rolling with godlike powers. When you wander into a tiger enclosure to catch a nap, or you're the one who can ride the horse that's 'too spirited' for anyone else to approach, or you swim with sharks, it's impossible for other people not to know that you're blessed.<br /> <br /> The cool factor alone is well worth the investment.<br /> <br /> That said, I don't see how folding in at least part of Leader of the Pack (the communication aspect anyway) would in any way be unfair of too much. I'd suggest that anything that allows you to affect their Attitude toward you may require a separate power that requires imbuing Legend but speaking to and being at no risk of harm from animals wrapped up together as an innate seems like a fair compromise.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2608-squee","name":"Squee","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2608_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"120"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-24T00:24:13-08:00","id":1276395,"title":"","content":"It\u2019s useful in the Jungle as insects and arachnids are a deadly pain, also useful for setting up traps where you stumble upon a swarm of bats or bees or sharks.<br /> <br /> So thing is while talking to Ghosts may seem useful more often, if you are immune to Beasts you can set up quite the advantage by actually using that to your advantage. Be Batman or Doctor Bees.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-24T21:42:54-08:00","id":1276560,"title":"","content":"See, yeah. Batman, while he doesn't do terribly much with bats makes me think of why the communication aspect might not be the best basic thing for Beasts. I suppose Spider-Man might be even better as he's got more spider features going on with him. Were Peter Parker a Hero level Scion I'd throw Beasts (Spider) with Animal Aspect for Spider Sense and probably Epic Strength out of somewhere. I've been working out a bounty hunter character with Beasts (Wolf) going on for Animal Aspect and potentially Tooth and Claw. His thing is more about being the wolf, metaphorically, than having legions of wolves at his beck and call.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3776-autodefenestrate","name":"AutoDefenestrate","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3776_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"120"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-24T22:05:38-08:00","id":1276563,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AutoDefenestrate</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1275411-beasts-innate-power?p=1276560#post1276560\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">See, yeah. Batman, while he doesn't do terribly much with bats makes me think of why the communication aspect might not be the best basic thing for Beasts. I suppose Spider-Man might be even better as he's got more spider features going on with him.</div> </div> </div> </div>I wouldn\u2019t give either of those characters the Beast Purview at all to be honest. Spider Sense would probably be an expression of Epic Dex heightening reflexes to superhuman levels in one of his Boons. The only spidery thing he does that isn\u2019t Epic Dex or Epic Strength are the webs, and that\u2019s a feature power of relics.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-25T06:00:37-08:00","id":1276615,"title":"","content":"They may have access to spider and bat motifs tho but yeah i agree they don't have access to the beast purview.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Completed campaign: Scion 2nd Edition. Les L\u00e9gendes Currently playing: Being a dad for a 3 year old daughter and a 2 years old son and now a beautiful new baby.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11312-maitrecorbo","name":"Maitrecorbo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11312_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"719"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-25T06:33:25-08:00","id":1276620,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1275411-beasts-innate-power?p=1276563#post1276563\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I wouldn\u2019t give either of those characters the Beast Purview at all to be honest. Spider Sense would probably be an expression of Epic Dex heightening reflexes to superhuman levels in one of his Boons. The only spidery thing he does that isn\u2019t Epic Dex or Epic Strength are the webs, and that\u2019s a feature power of relics.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Actually, Spidey Sense would be Epic Perception, since he doesn't even have to know where the threat is coming from in order for it to warn him. Not only that, but it warns him of danger <i>just before it strikes</i>, not during the attack.<br /> <br /> And according to Death Battle, it gives him omniscient awareness of his surroundings. Which explains how he's able to sling his webs and perform his crazy acrobatics without even having to look where he's going.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-25T06:44:09-08:00","id":1276624,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1275411-beasts-innate-power?p=1276620#post1276620\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Actually, Spidey Sense would be Epic Perception.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not a thing at the moment.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-25T07:46:38-08:00","id":1276635,"title":"","content":"Hm. Spidey sense would be tricky. I feel that it would work as a knack. There is a guardian knack that gives bonus against dangers. But i could see it fit thematically with knacks from the sage calling (master of the world i think, i don't have access to the pdf at the moment) and maybe the hunter calling.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Completed campaign: Scion 2nd Edition. Les L\u00e9gendes Currently playing: Being a dad for a 3 year old daughter and a 2 years old son and now a beautiful new baby.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11312-maitrecorbo","name":"Maitrecorbo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11312_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"719"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-25T14:10:04-08:00","id":1276689,"title":"","content":"Yeah, I can see how neither don't really have the purview. I was mostly running off the mention of <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar754_2.gif');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"754\" data-vbnamecard=\"754\">Eldagusto</a> of Batman and I figured Spider-Man seemed more like one who ran with Beasts over Bats. <br /> <br /> But I'd definitely say that a superhero like Spider-Man falls into the Guardian calling. For the most part Spidey's focus is on saving the people over fighting the big monsters. His tendency to crack wise almost makes me want to give him Trickster too, but I'm not sure I'd really put that in for him, and depending on how hard you're laying on his scientific achievements he could be a Creator or Sage, I suppose. Anyway, I guess this isn't a Stat a fictional character thread.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3776-autodefenestrate","name":"AutoDefenestrate","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3776_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"120"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-25T15:08:28-08:00","id":1276696,"title":"","content":"Yeah that sounds like a good spidey analysis, he is epic dex with emphasis on agility over speed, though he is hella fast. And 10 ton strength range.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-25T18:56:49-08:00","id":1276722,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eldagusto</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1275411-beasts-innate-power?p=1276696#post1276696\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah that sounds like a good spidey analysis, he is epic dex with emphasis on agility over speed, though he is hella fast. And 10 ton strength range.</div> </div> </div> </div>I did a write of him a while ago (not shared on the forums, waiting for appropeite thread). I did give him Animal Aspect (wallcrawling, I think), but his abilities were generally emulated through other means. Epic Dex, Epic Str and the Guardian calling represent his powers. Beast (Spiders) is mostly there for flavour and the extra motif.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thoughts ripple out, birthing others","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1624-falleneco","name":"FallenEco","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1624_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1927"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-26T23:32:37-08:00","id":1276964,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1275411-beasts-innate-power?p=1275683#post1275683\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Specialization limits the usefulness of everything else in a purview (in return for the Motif). Why would the Innate be different from all the Boons or possible Marvels in that regard?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> This isn't true for Beast. Specializing Beast only limits Marvels and Boons that let you take on animal characteristics. Of the Boons listed in Hero, this specifically leaves out the one that lets you talk to any animal.<br /> <br /> It is specifically less limiting than Artistry and Passion. And those two call out Marvels and Boons as the only things limited by specializing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1178-ravenmancer","name":"Ravenmancer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"36"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-27T02:28:29-08:00","id":1276973,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ravenmancer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1275411-beasts-innate-power?p=1276964#post1276964\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> This isn't true for Beast. Specializing Beast only limits Marvels and Boons that let you take on animal characteristics. Of the Boons listed in Hero, this specifically leaves out the one that lets you talk to any animal.<br /> <br /> It is specifically less limiting than Artistry and Passion. And those two call out Marvels and Boons as the only things limited by specializing.</div> </div> </div> </div>So this got brought up with Neall on the Discord... When asked if, say, Leader of the Pack would apply to all animals even if you take the Specialized Purview.<br /> <br /> His answer was, and I quote, &quot;I don't see why not&quot;.<br /> <br /> This... Opens the door to MANY possibilities.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Disclaimer: In favor of fun and enjoyment, but may speak up to warn you that you're gonna step on a metaphorical land mine","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","name":"Kyman201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2142_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-27T13:44:26-08:00","id":1277070,"title":"","content":"What if the innate bonus was modified to apply to animals of a lower tier regardless of legendary status? Then at least it would apply to magical animals but would still allow for dramatic battles with powerful creatures.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13508-necrobotany","name":"necrobotany","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}